This code provides a locale-independent string-to-floating-point conversion routine for C.

Unlike the standard C library functions, these routines do not depend on the current locale and therefore parse decimal points consistently.

Files included:

* str2dbl.h
  Public header file.

* str2dbl.c
  Implementation source file.

* test-str2dbl.c
  Test program source file.

* test-str2dbl.txt
  Test pattern file used by the test program.

Provided functions:

* str2dbl
  Converts a null-terminated string to a double, similar to the standard C function `strtod`.

* strn2dbl
  Same as `str2dbl`, but takes an explicit string length.

* str2dbl_noexp / strn2dbl_noexp
  Variants of `str2dbl` / `strn2dbl` that do not accept exponent notation.

* str2flt / strn2flt / str2flt_noexp / strn2flt_noexp
  Single-precision (float) versions of the above functions.
